{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790959045,"nonce":"C4F/2g8ucG29BbxbFOf20wtLyQw=","title":"Deferred snapshot bodies: readers that use module.functions get the signature shell, so Python programs segfault or compute wrong values","message":"Since 2a0e3a1d (\"Decode snapshot function bodies on demand\", 3b7f29cd45b2936dcf15efb81290127592246532d527eb6c6f19c1b85ebc7ce9), a closed program's linked library functions are signature shells in the module and their bodies are decoded from the snapshot on demand. tier_body, Scratch::add and FunctionEntry::body read through the snapshot source; other readers still take module.functions.get(id) and see a shell with no blocks.\n\nReproducers (NUC, release, llvm-backend, ZYPY_LLVM=1, tiered; both correct with ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD=1):\n- crates/zyntax_python/conformance/inference/function_as_value.py: outer() returning inner() that calls double(s) on a captured \"a\" prints an empty line instead of \"aa\".\n- crates/zyntax_python/conformance/modules/operator_functools.py: total() over functools.reduce(operator.add, ...) segfaults (exit 139).\nBisect over ff51664c..7e2e935c: 351efdd5 good, 2a0e3a1d bad. These are the macOS and Windows CI failures on origin/main since 2026-09-29.\n\nSetting defer_prelowered_bodies to false in TieredRuntime makes Python conformance (both warm-up modes) and gate.py (tiered and Cranelift-first-call) pass. Deferral comes back once every reader of a function body (interpreter, inliner, release facts, OSR, LLVM promotion, Cranelift lazy stubs) goes through one accessor that decodes the snapshot source, with these two cases as regression tests.","files":null}]}